{
    "pageid": 2852,
    "title": "Ambition events",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Rulers can try to raise an attribute that is below 8 by selecting an appropriate objective and waiting for random ambition events to fire. Without Way of Life , this takes the form of an ambition to reach 8."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "With Way of Life , these events instead require having a related focus , and having the attribute be below 8 even with the focus. The \"+3\" focus tends to have more such events: for example, war focus has five while hunting focus has one. (Each focus also provides ways to improve its attribute that do not require the attribute to be below 8.)"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Each of the event chains can only be taken once per character, and only one event chain can be active at a time."
                }
            ]
        },
